      "evidence": [
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "`BS0` (pin 10) -> GND; `BS1` (pin 11) -> VCC; `BS2` (pin 12) -> GND ... That BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0 strapping ... is the SSD1306's documented I2C-mode pin configuration."},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "display.kicad_sch: U4 BS0/BS1/BS2 (pins 10/11/12) wired to the VCC and GND symbols near the top-right of U4"}
      ],
      "impact": "The display controller is placed in a non-I2C (SPI/parallel) interface mode, so the 2-wire DISP_SCL/DISP_SDA bus cannot communicate with it and the OLED would remain blank.",
      "confidence": 0.33
    }
  ],
  "summary": "All component values, types and the documented NFC/display/touch connections match the specification, but the SSD1306 interface-select strapping on the display sheet does not appear to match the specified I2C configuration (BS2,BS1,BS0 = 0,1,0), which would put the display driver into the wrong interface mode."
}

